# Read automatically by the globally-installed gorun binary (see
# loadDotEnv in cmd/gorun/main.go) before it resolves .gorun/config.yaml -
# so DB_MYSQL_PASSWORD below satisfies the ${DB_MYSQL_PASSWORD} reference
# there without you having to export it by hand. A real exported
# environment variable always overrides whatever's in this file.
#
# internal/config/config.go's MySQLPassword() reads this same variable
# directly via os.Getenv - it does not read this file itself, only gorun
# does, and only when gorun's own process is what's running.
#
# Empty here because local MySQL's root user has no password. Never
# commit a real password to a file like this one in an actual project.
DB_MYSQL_PASSWORD=
